Methodology source / attribution
=================================

The worker methodology skills in this directory:

  brainstorming.md
  writing-plans.md
  test-driven-development.md
  systematic-debugging.md
  verification-before-completion.md
  requesting-code-review.md
  receiving-code-review.md

are TERSE, Turing-flavored translations of skills from the "superpowers"
project by Jesse Vincent (obra/superpowers):

  https://github.com/obra/superpowers
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Jesse Vincent

superpowers is the single source of execution discipline for the Turing OS
multi-agent workflow. These translations adapt the original skills to the
worker toolset (read_file, write_file, execute_terminal_command, ticket and
document tools) and drop Claude-Code-only mechanics (the Skill tool, TodoWrite,
git worktrees, plan-mode, and subagent/parallel-dispatch). All cross-worker
flow (e.g. code review) is relayed Worker -> PM -> Worker; workers never
communicate peer-to-peer.

The methodology and structure originate with superpowers; credit for that
work belongs to Jesse Vincent under the MIT License above.
